        Automated Network Health & Latency Probing Script for Remote Teams
      </h2>
      <p>
        Prior to committing to a long-term apartment lease or coliving contract in Da Nang, run this automated network diagnostic tool from your terminal. It executes concurrent latency benchmarks to AWS Singapore, AWS US-West, and Cloudflare DNS, tracking jitter and packet drops:
      </p>

      <pre is:raw class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl text-xs font-mono text-emerald-400 overflow-x-auto border border-slate-800"><code>#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Da Nang Remote Worker Network Diagnostic Probe
set -euo pipefail

echo "========================================================"
echo " Starting Network Quality &amp; Jitter Probe: Da Nang, VN"
echo "========================================================"

TARGET_SG="ap-southeast-1.compute.amazonaws.com"
TARGET_US="us-west-2.compute.amazonaws.com"
TARGET_CF="1.1.1.1"

probe_target() {
    local host="$1"
    local name="$2"
    echo -n "Probing $name ($host)... "
    local ping_result
    ping_result=$(ping -c 10 -q "$host" 2&gt;&amp;1) || {
        echo "FAILED to reach $host"
        return
    }
    
    local rtt_stats
    rtt_stats=$(echo "$ping_result" | awk -F'/' 'END {print $4, $5, $6}')
    local loss
    loss=$(echo "$ping_result" | grep -o '[0-9]*% packet loss')
    
    echo "Done! Latency (min/avg/max): $rtt_stats ms | Packet Loss: $loss"
}

probe_target "$TARGET_SG" "AWS Singapore Hub"
probe_target "$TARGET_US" "AWS US-West Hub"
probe_target "$TARGET_CF" "Cloudflare Edge DNS"

echo "--------------------------------------------------------"
echo "DNS Resolution Benchmark:"
for dns in "1.1.1.1" "8.8.8.8" "203.113.131.1"; do
    resolve_time=$(dig @$dns google.com +stats | grep "Query time:" | awk '{print $4, $5}')
    echo "  DNS $dns response time: $resolve_time"
done

echo "========================================================"
echo " Probe complete! Verify avg latency: SG &lt; 40ms, US &lt; 180ms"
echo "========================================================"
</code></pre>

